---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import RangingHero from '../instruments/RangingHero.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base title="Research" description="UWB localization research: custom DS-TWR ranging firmware, channel and preamble tuning, validated to 0.4% error over 10,000 m² with a total station.">
  <div class="container prose-page">
    <header class="res-head">
      <RangingHero />
      <p class="label">/research · Krishna Defence & Allied Industries · IIT Gandhinagar · May – Jul 2025</p>
      <h1>Centimeter-level UWB localization at industrial scale</h1>
      <p class="res-abstract">
        <strong>Abstract.</strong> Autonomous vehicles in naval dockyards need
        position estimates that survive steel, cranes, and GPS denial across
        200 × 200 m. We replaced encoder-based localization with Ultra-Wideband
        trilateration, wrote a custom Double-Sided Two-Way Ranging protocol to
        break the stock firmware's 45 m ceiling, and validated the system
        against a surveyor's total station: <strong>0.4% error over a
        10,000 m² operational area</strong>, with stable ranging at 315 m.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>1 · Sensor selection</h2>
      <p>
        Candidates evaluated: Bluetooth, LoRaWAN, RFID, NFC, radar, CCTV-based
        tracking, IR, and hyperspectral approaches. UWB won on the only axes
        that mattered — accuracy at range without line-of-sight guarantees, and
        infrastructure that a working dockyard can actually install. Hardware:
        <strong>Qorvo DWM3001CDK</strong> development kits as tags and anchors.
      </p>

      <h2>2 · System</h2>
      <p>
        Prototype platform: Raspberry Pi 4B running ROS, a DWM3001CDK tag, a
        9-DOF IMU for orientation, and a differential-drive base. SLAM and NAV2
        run on top of the localization layer; in the LIDAR-equipped
        configuration, UWB and LIDAR estimates are fused.
      </p>

      <h2>3 · Staged validation</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>2 × 2 m indoor</strong> — trilateration correctness</li>
        <li><strong>7 × 7 m outdoor</strong> — UWB + IMU only; no encoders, no LIDAR</li>
        <li><strong>50 × 60 m, IIT Gandhinagar</strong> — ground truth from a
        surveyor's total station, not our own estimator</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>4 · The firmware: DS-TWR beyond 45 m</h2>
      <p>
        Stock ranging firmware capped at 45 m. We implemented our own
        <strong>Double-Sided Two-Way Ranging (DS-TWR)</strong> protocol and
        re-derived the physical-layer configuration per range profile:
        switching between <strong>channel 5 and channel 9</strong>, tuning
        <strong>preamble length and PAC size</strong>, and re-budgeting the
        ranging <strong>time delays</strong> (poll-TX→response-RX and the rest
        of the exchange schedule) for each configuration.
      </p>

      <table>
        <caption class="label">Measured range–accuracy trade across configurations</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Profile</th>
            <th scope="col">Preamble</th>
            <th scope="col">Range</th>
            <th scope="col">Accuracy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Short</td><td>128</td><td>~10 m</td><td>±2 cm</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Mid</td><td>256</td><td>~50 m</td><td>±10 cm</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Long</td><td>512</td><td>315 m</td><td>±40 cm (50 × 50 m)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        The trade is physics: longer preambles buy detection range and cost
        update rate. There is no "best" configuration — there is a correct one
        per operating area, which is why the tuning had to be ours.
      </p>

      <h2>5 · Results</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>±2 cm accuracy in areas up to 10 × 10 m</li>
        <li>Stable communication at 315 m after the firmware rewrite</li>
        <li><strong>0.4% localization error across 10,000 m²</strong>, total-station validated</li>
        <li>SLAM + NAV2 autonomous navigation running on the localization layer</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Full build narrative, footage, and field tests:
        <a href={`${base}/fleet/kdail/`}>the KDAIL case study</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style>
    .res-head {
      position: relative;
      padding-top: var(--sp-12);
    }
    .res-head > :global(*:not(canvas)) {
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
    }
    .res-abstract {
      font-size: var(--text-md);
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      max-width: var(--measure);
      border-left: 2px solid var(--signal);
      padding-left: var(--sp-4);
    }
    caption { text-align: left; padding-bottom: var(--sp-2); }
  </style>
</Base>
